Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 13:59:58 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09832/11362] [outer-loop] Un-retire exp6581; correct both
 manifest entries

Corrects commit 613d227da1, which retired two tasks on evidence that only
supported retiring one, and named a cause that does not exist.

EXP6581 IS UN-RETIRED. retire_if_same_verdict requires the same verdict on a
REPEAT run. The conductor journal shows 0 launches for the Qwen3.6 task and
2 for the Gemma-4-31B task. Exp6581 ran once and never repeated, so it never
met the condition. Removed from scripts/conductor_exclusion_manifest.json
and verified free through ExclusionManifest.is_excluded(): 6581 False, 6582
True, control False.

The "10 poison-and-rerun events" figure in the prior commit was wrong. It
came from a grep matching poisoned.*658[12]|one-family flagship, which also
counts commit lines and in-process-doc lines. The real rerun count is two,
both Exp6582. I put that number in a commit message as justification for
retiring a scope.

NO PRECONDITION FAILED. Both artifacts record
gate_check_summary.all_structured_gates_passed=true with first_failure=null,
aggregate_row_recomputation.authentic_terminal_row_count=0, and
preconditions_checked absent. Every structured gate passed. The run produced
zero authentic terminal rows and honestly declined to make a quality claim.
The prior reason text read the verdict STRING,
blocked_precondition_failed_without_quality_claim, and asserted a failing
quality precondition from the words in it without opening the artifact. Two
model families reaching the same verdict was real; the mechanism I inferred
from it was not.

That changes the open question. Not "why does the quality precondition
fail", but "why does a 15-40 minute live run produce zero authentic terminal
rows". The diagnosis agent has been redirected.

The wrong reason text is KEPT VERBATIM in both files, with the correction
appended beside it, per never-prune. A reader needs to see what was believed
and when it changed. The YAML entry gains correction_2026_08_24 and
un_retired_experiment_ids; experiment_ids now names only Exp6582.

Exp6582 stays retired on its own evidence: two runs, same verdict, 1109s
then 2411s of live GPU, in a poison-and-rerun loop with no exit.

